# Rendered pages that present the entity list, and why each is allowed.
#
# Format: <url>   # why this one is allowed
#
# A page here is NOT automatically wrong. A page GENERATED from the producer is
# the producer rendered, and that is the correct way to show the list to a
# person. What this sweep catches is the other kind — a list typed by hand into
# a marketing page, which nothing updates when a type is added or renamed.
#
# The two cannot be told apart from the outside: generated HTML and copied HTML
# look identical. So each allowed page states WHICH it is and where it derives
# from, and that sentence is the thing a reviewer checks.
#
# This list may FALL or hold. It may never RISE without a human deciding so in
# the same PR that adds the page.

https://orangecat.ch/docs  # generated: src/app/(public)/docs/page.tsx maps ENTITY_TYPES from the registry, filtering only `wallet` as infrastructure. Verified 2026-09-17 — it renders 14 names and the registry has 15.
